# Netlify redirect rules.
#
# ONE JOB: send the .netlify.app hostname to the custom domain, so the site does
# not answer 200 at two addresses with byte-identical documents. Star Stuff found
# that shape on 2026-08-15 and queering.earth had it the day its domain attached.
#
# ENABLED 2026-09-19, the day the domain resolved. Verified before uncommenting:
# stimpunks.love answers 200, www.stimpunks.love and http:// both 301 to the apex,
# and the netlify.app hostname was still answering 200 with the same document —
# which is the duplicate-address problem these two lines exist to close.
#
# Before that they stayed commented on purpose: redirecting the only working
# hostname to one that does not resolve is a site that is simply down, which is
# why queering.earth kept its own commented until 2026-09-07.

https://stimpunks-love.netlify.app/*  https://stimpunks.love/:splat  301!
http://stimpunks-love.netlify.app/*   https://stimpunks.love/:splat  301!
